  os_infra_finding: {'persona': 'os-infra-primitivist', 'candidate': 'Use OS file-system watch hooks (CAP-222 macOS File-Hook Example) to trigger graph execution on worktree changes, replacing shell-diff polling with native inotify/FSEvents boundaries.', 'solution_class': 'process-boundary', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'CAP-222, CAP-254 Session Worktree Lifecycle, does_the_platform_already_do_this', 'is_this_a_graph': 'yes', 'effort_risk': 'medium/high. Requires kernel-level hook integration and cross-platform abstraction; eliminates polling overhead but adds OS-specific failure modes.', 'rationale': 'The problem witnesses shell-diff context driving hook solutions; OS permissions and process boundaries were never considered despite existing in the repo. File-system watch primitives (inotify, FSEvents) are already enforced by the kernel and eliminate the 601-line hook cost by delegating to the platform.'}
  data_process_finding: {'persona': 'data-process-planner', 'candidate': 'Require solution-class classification at FR intake before author context loads, dissolving shell/hook bias before planning begins.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-806-author-sh-brief-preflight.md; ask_before_generate; does_the_platform_already_do_this', 'is_this_a_graph': 'Yes. The intake checklist becomes a decision graph routing to os-permissions, process-boundary, or graph-pipeline before author shell/hook context primes the planner.', 'effort_risk': 'Low. Adds one classification step to FR schema validation gate (CAP-108, CAP-116). Reuses existing preflight pattern from FR-806.', 'rationale': "Witnessed incidents show planner bias follows author's loaded context (shell→shell, hooks→hooks). Intake-time classification closes input shape before planning fires, preventing 601-line hook and 5-round review cycles. Dissolves the problem at schema boundary."}
  yamlgraph_native_finding: {'persona': 'yamlgraph-native-planner', 'candidate': 'Invoke research-route graph (FR-890 closed-input alternatives route) to fan out orthogonal planner personas across solution classes: os-permissions, process-boundary, schema-data, graph-pipeline, subtraction, external-method, boundary-enforcement. Deterministic collection of graph shapes feeds map judgement per class, reducing findings into structured alternatives table.', 'solution_class': 'graph-pipeline', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-890, research-route graph, CAP-248 invocation-time tool-slot binding, is_this_a_graph Scripture trap', 'is_this_a_graph': 'research-route: closed-input alternatives route with deterministic collection, fan-out map per persona, and reducer-driven alternatives table. Matches committed shape exactly.', 'effort_risk': 'Low/medium. The graph exists and is proven; binding solution-class personas as tool slots (CAP-249) is the only novel seam. Estimated 2–3 hours to wire planner personas and validate output shape.', 'rationale': 'The problem names the exact failure mode: author context (shell, hooks) narrows solution search before alternatives are explored. research-route is purpose-built to prevent this by running orthogonal planners in parallel and merging their findings deterministically. Avoids the 601-line hook and 5-round review cycle by surfacing all seven solution classes upfront.'}
  subtractionist_finding: {'persona': 'subtractionist', 'candidate': 'Delete the requirement to auto-propose solutions from shell/hook context. Instead, mandate explicit solution-class declaration upfront, forcing authors to consider all available frameworks (house, shell, hooks, graph-pipeline) before planning begins.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-806-author-sh-brief-preflight.md; CAP-237 Author Brief Pre-Flight; Scripture: ask_before_generate, does_the_platform_already_do_this', 'is_this_a_graph': 'Yes. Solution-class selection is a routing decision; a graph node can enforce declaration before dispatch to solution-bearing FRs.', 'effort_risk': 'Low. Adds one schema field and one validation gate; no new automation. Reuses existing CAP-237 preflight pattern and FR-806 enforcement model.', 'rationale': 'The 2026-08-25 incident shows context-driven solution selection (shell in diff → shell solution) bypassed OS-permissions class entirely. Forcing explicit declaration at brief intake closes the input-closure gap without adding daemon or review rounds.'}
